<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jean-Andoche Junot</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1771">1771</a>–<a href="/years/1813">1813</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Duke of Abrantes</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jean-Andoche Junot was a French general and early comrade of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon Bonaparte</a>. In November 1807 he led the invasion of Portugal, reaching <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> just after the royal court had sailed for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, and was made Duke of Abrantes. Defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arthur-wellesley-1st-duke-of-wellington">Arthur Wellesley</a> at Vimeiro in August 1808, he evacuated Portugal under the Convention of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sintra">Sintra</a>. He later served in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and died in 1813.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jean-andoche-junot.jpg" alt="Jean-Andoche Junot" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andrea Appiani · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Junot,_par_Appiani.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
